<h1>Chapter 4: Implementation & Testing</h1>

<h2>4.1 Development Details</h2>
<p>The MARG backend is organized into modular packages:</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>in.marg.spatial</code>: Ellipsoidal projection (Wgs84UtmProjection), metric point representations (MetricPoint), and bounding box transformations.</li>
    <li><code>in.marg.routing</code>: GreenfieldAStarRouter, CompositeCostSurface, 13 CostLayer implementations, TradeOffEvaluationService, and AlignmentPreference records.</li>
    <li><code>in.marg.transport</code>: HighwayNetworkPlannerService, HubEvaluationService, and IRC interchange placement models.</li>
    <li><code>in.marg.row</code>: RightOfWayCorridorEngine for multi-stage corridor buffering (60 m direct RoW, 100 m construction zone, 250 m environmental buffer).</li>
    <li><code>in.marg.wildlife</code>: IndianWildlifeSanctuaryRegistry and statutory clearance evaluation engines.</li>
    <li><code>in.marg.region</code>: RegionalCorridorRegistry managing two-tier corridor loading semantics.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4.2 Experimental Setup</h2>
<p><b>Hardware:</b> AMD Ryzen 7 / Intel Core i7 8-Core Host @ 3.8 GHz, 16 GB DDR4 RAM @ 3200 MHz, 512 GB NVMe SSD (Read/Write &approx; 3200 MB/s).<br>
<b>Software:</b> Windows 11 Enterprise (64-bit), Java 25 Early-Access VM (-Xms2g -Xmx6g -XX:+UseG1GC), Node.js v20.18.0 LTS, Apache Maven 3.9.9.</p>

