<h2>4.4 Safety Measures</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>Coordinate Input Validation:</b> All coordinates submitted via API endpoints are strictly validated against India's national geographic envelope (6.5&deg;N &le; lat &le; 37.5&deg;N, 68.0&deg;E &le; lon &le; 97.5&deg;E). Out-of-bounds coordinates return HTTP 400 Bad Request.</li>
    <li><b>DoS Mitigation:</b> Search windows are capped at 0.35&deg; buffer margin, maximum corridor distance is capped at 800 km, and node evaluations are subject to a hard 25,000 iteration ceiling.</li>
    <li><b>CORS Hardening:</b> Cross-Origin Resource Sharing is strictly constrained in CorsConfig.java to authorized origin domains and local Vite development ports.</li>
    <li><b>Data Provenance Integrity:</b> Satellite tiles and remote sensing rasters are verified with SHA-256 local checksum caching to prevent upstream data tampering.</li>
</ul>

